uang</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Jensen Huang</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Artificial intelligence</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Computer Chip</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Computers and the Internet</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Tech Industry</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Adultery</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Spying and Intelligence Agencies</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Corporate espionage</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">China</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Alice Huang</category><media:content url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/11/15/multimedia/14bizsun-huang-valley-03-lpmz/14bizsun-huang-valley-03-lpmz-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600.jpg" medium="image"><media:credit>via Reuters</media:credit><media:description>The revelation that Jensen Huang had a romantic relationship with Alice Huang changed the chatter in Silicon Valley from soaring I.P.O.s to tawdry affairs.</media:description></media:content></item><item><title>California Sues OpenAI Over A.I. Safety Issues</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/16/technology/california-openai-ai-safety.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/16/technology/california-openai-ai-safety.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</guid><atom:link rel="standout" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/16/technology/california-openai-ai-safety.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss" /><description>The state attorney general filed a lawsuit accusing the company of failing to put appropriate safeguards on