-heyitsyoon.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</guid><atom:link rel="standout" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/06/technology/tiktok-time-saved-videos-heyitsyoon.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss" /><description>Videos on social media often save key details for the end. One content creator, who goes by Heyitsyoon, skips the filler so viewers don’t have to wait.</description><dc:creator>Victor Mather</dc:creator><pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 10:00:58 GMT</pubDate><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Social Media</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">TikTok</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Video Recordings</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Downloads and Streaming</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Computers and the Internet</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Tech Industry</category><media:content url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/10/28/multimedia/00xp-time-saver-promo/00xp-time-saver-promo-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600.jpg" medium="image" /></item><item><title>Trump Administration Moves to Close A.I. Chip Loophole Ahead of China Trip</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/16/us/politics/trump-china-ai-chip-loophole.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/16/us/politics/trump-china-ai-chip-loophole.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</guid><atom:link rel="standout" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/16/us/politics/trump-china-ai-chip-loophole.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss" /><description>The rules have been a topic of fierce debate in the administration and would cut back on a booming data center business serving Chinese companies.</description><dc:creator>Ana Swanson and Tony Romm</dc:creator><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 13:49:19 GMT</pubDate><category domain="http://ww