m/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Jamieson Greer</category><media:content url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/11/16/multimedia/16dc-remote-access-01-bfgz/16dc-remote-access-01-bfgz-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600.jpg" medium="image"><media:credit>Ulet Ifansasti for The New York Times</media:credit><media:description>A Megaspeed data center under construction in Johor, Malaysia.</media:description></media:content></item><item><title>Inside Microsoft’s Rush to Get Back Online After a Global Outage</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/13/business/microsoft-outage.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/13/business/microsoft-outage.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</guid><atom:link rel="standout" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/13/business/microsoft-outage.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss" /><description>A prolonged outage left many without email and other services, the most recent reminder that the world’s technological underpinnings rely on just a few companies.</description><dc:creator>Karen Weise</dc:creator><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:28:58 GMT</pubDate><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Microsoft</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Network Outages</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Email</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Software</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Cloud computing</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Artificial intelligence</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Engineering</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Computers and the Internet</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Tech Industry</category><media:content url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/11/13/multimedia/13biz-microsoft-down-ptmz/13biz-microsoft-down-ptmz-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600.jpg" medium="image"><media:credit>Grant Hindsley for The New York Times</media:credit><media:description>Microsoft acknowledged that about 20 different services were impaired by the outage.</media:description></media:content></item><item><title>Amazon Kindle Colorsoft Review: The Single-Task Gadget of Our Times</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/05/technology/personaltech/amazon-kindle-colorsoft-review.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/05/technology/personaltech/amazon-kindle-colorsoft-review.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</guid><atom:link rel="standout" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/05/technology/personaltech/amazon-kindle-colorsoft-review.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss" /><description>E-book reader sales are soaring as consumers seek technology offering respite from social media and artificial intelligence hype. It’s even better in color.</description><dc:creator>Brian X. Chen</dc:creator><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 10:03:28 GMT</pubDate><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">EBooks EReaders</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Kindle</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Amazon</category><media:content url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/11/04/multimedia/04biz-techfix-1-02-jlmg/04biz-techfix-1-02-jlmg-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600.jpg" medium="image"><media:credit>Manuel Orbegozo for The New York Times</media:credit></media:content></item><item><title>How Sam Bankman-Fried Lost Out on a $35 Billion Jackpot From Anthropic</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/16/technology/sam-bankman-fried-anthropic.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/16/technology/sam-bankman-fried-anthropic.html?