dit><media:description>Sam Bankman-Fried, founder of the crypto firm FTX, leaving federal court in Manhattan in 2022. He was convicted of fraud and is now in federal prison in California.</media:description></media:content></item><item><title>Jensen Huang Says He Would Return as Nvidia CEO if Asked</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/17/technology/jensen-huang-nvidia-statement.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/17/technology/jensen-huang-nvidia-statement.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</guid><atom:link rel="standout" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/17/technology/jensen-huang-nvidia-statement.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss" /><description>Mr. Huang resigned as chief executive of the company last week after revelations that he had affairs with an employee and a woman linked to Chinese intelligence.</description><dc:creator>Kalley Huang</dc:creator><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 16:21:23 GMT</pubDate><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Jen-Hsun Huang</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Jensen Huang</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">NVIDIA</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Board of directors</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Corporate espionage</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Appointments and Executive Changes</category><media:content url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/11/17/multimedia/17biz-jensen-statement-vhjm/17biz-jensen-statement-vhjm-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600.jpg" medium="image"><media:credit>Eric Lee for The New York Times</media:credit><media:description>Jensen Huang, the former chief executive of Nvidia.</media:description></media:content></item><item><title>Fan Fiction Site AO3 Returns, and So Do Its Readers, in Droves</title><lin